* Phase N (decision 2026-10-24): pins the equal-time order of the pending entries (time, then the
* smaller wavelength first). 3-ring CROW, 4 channels on a 100 GHz grid pulsed together
* (tests/bench/crow_gen.py 3 --nwl 4 --pulses 1 --duration 4e-10 --traceall 0 --probes 0), default
* tolerances, MLPROBEs on the bus (through), inside ring 2 (r2b_out) and at the drop. The channels share
* the delays, so each port holds several wavelengths per time step and emits them in successive delta
* cycles; with zero-delay coupler paths, the per-wavelength values depend on that order at tolerance level
* (B-198): against the former |E| order, 1551.2 nm moves by up to 9e-5 of its peak, the others are
* identical. A change of the equal-time order shows here.
VLSRC1 in values=[[0,0.001,1.55120301459e-06],[0,0.001,1.55040079748e-06],[0,0.001,1.54959940969e-06],[0,0.001,1.54879884993e-06],[1e-09,0,1.55120301459e-06],[1e-09,0,1.55040079748e-06],[1e-09,0,1.54959940969e-06],[1e-09,0,1.54879884993e-06]]
COUPLER0 in r1b_out through r1a_in kp=0.15
COUPLER1 r1a_out r2b_out r1b_in r2a_in kp=0.15
COUPLER2 r2a_out r3b_out r2b_in r3a_in kp=0.15
COUPLER3 r3a_out add r3b_in drop kp=0.15
WG1a r1a_in r1a_out L=3.96409238e-05 att=2 neff=2.2 ng=4.3
WG1b r1b_in r1b_out L=4.0447228e-05 att=2 neff=2.2 ng=4.3
